2014 so I will treat the design as documentation, not as something I need to execute now.\\n\\n**Likely canonical entry points** (the ones I would pin; please confirm versions):\\n- JaxMARL: `from jaxmarl.environments.mpe import SimpleSpread` (class registered under name `\\\"MPE_SimpleSpread\\\"` via `jaxmarl.make_env` / `jaxmarl.register`). Constructor params I expect: `num_agents`, `num_landmarks`, `max_cycles`, `action_type` or `continuous_actions`, optional `key`, optional `batch_size` via external `jax.vmap` (no built-in `batch_size` kwarg in the env itself).\\n- PettingZoo MPE: `from pettingzoo.mpe import simple_spread_v3` for the continuous-action version, or `simple_spread_v2` for discrete. Use the `parallel_env` interface (`reset()`, `step(action_dict)`, `.agents`, `.observation_spaces`, `.action_spaces`) so both sides model \\\"all agents stepped per world-step\\\". AEC isn't directly comparable.\\n\\n**Version-specific knobs I'd lock down before designing further**:\\n- Action space parity: PettingZoo default `continuous_actions=True` (action `Box(0,1,(5,))`), discrete when `continuous_actions=False` (`Discrete(5)`). The JaxMARL MPE port has historically been discrete; newer JaxMARL (0.1.x) exposes both \\u2014 needs explicit confirmation, since for a fair random-action SPS comparison the action-dimension shape must match so per-step compute cost isn't lopsided.\\n- Default counts: PettingZoo `simple_spread` defaults to 3 agents, 3 landmarks, `max_cycles=25`, `local_ratio=0.5`. JaxMARL should mirror these \\u2014 confirm the `SimpleSpread(...)` defaults match.\\n- JaxMARL batching: it is **not** auto-batched. Parallel envs are produced externally with `jax.vmap(env.step)`. Auto-reset, when used, must be opted into (typical pattern: `lax.scan` with a manual reset branch).\\n- PettingZoo auto-reset: manual between episodes; `parallel_env` does not auto-reset on `terminated/truncated`.\\n\\n## 2. Proposed approach (high-level)\\n\\n**Single matched-random-policy benchmark** where the only varying axis is the simulator stack.\\n\\n- **Environments** (matched):\\n  - `jaxmarl.environments.mpe.SimpleSpread(num_agents=N, num_landmarks=N, max_cycles=T, action_type=...continuous|discrete)` \\u2014 run on **JAX CPU** (no GPU available).\\n  - `pettingzoo.mpe.simple_spread_v{2|3}.parallel_env(N=..., max_cycles=T, continuous_actions=...)` \\u2014 driven from a single Python process, single env.\\n- **Sweep**: agent count `N \\u2208 {3 (default), 6, 9}`; action flavour `continuous` vs `discrete` (toggled if both stacks support it). `max_cycles=T = 25` (stock default).\\n- **Policy**: identical seeded per-step uniform random action sampler (`numpy.random.default_rng(seed)` for PettingZoo; `jax.random.split` key for JaxMARL) so neither stack benefits from \\\"smarter\\\" sampling. Pre-sample the full episode's actions in one action-array per stack to keep the action generator outside the timed region.\\n- **Loop shape, run on both**:\\n  - **Mode A \\u2014 Python loop (apples-to-apples)**: `for _ in range(T): env.step(actions)`. Time only the loop body. This matches PettingZoo's natural usage and quantifies JAX's per-call host\\u2194device overhead.\\n  - **Mode B \\u2014 `jax.lax.scan` rollout (JAX fast path)**: jit-compiled single-env scan over the `step` closure; report separately. This is the \\\"headline\\\" JAX throughput number and is the one to cite as JaxMARL's intrinsic capability.\\n- **Episode budget**: `E = 200` episodes per configuration per trial, with the **first 5 episodes discarded as warm-up** (to absorb JAX trace + compile + caches), so all reported numbers are warm-start steady-state.\\n- **Trials**: `R = 5` independent trials per cell, distinct outer seeds. Report mean \\u00b1 std and per-trial min/max.\\n- **Metric (primary)**: **environment steps per second (SPS)** = `(T \\u00d7 E) / elapsed_seconds_in_timed_loop`, where a \\\"step\\\" is **one world-step (a single `env.step` call that advances every agent by one transition)**. Reset cost is excluded from the numerator (and reset itself is unwound from the timed region, except as a diagnostic).\\n- **Secondary diagnostics recorded each cell**:\\n  - 1st-step wall time (includes JAX compile / cache fill; reported separately, not folded into SPS).\\n  - Steady-state per-step latency mean / p50 / p95 / p99 across steps in the timed window.\\n  - JAX compile time (Mode B only) and resident memory delta (`tracemalloc` for Python side; `jax.live_arrays()` count on JAX side).\\n  - Per-episode throughput distribution to detect GC / allocator stalls.\\n\\n## 3. Assumptions and uncertainties (flagged \\u2014 would materially change the design)\\n\\nMaterial assumptions I'm making because they aren't stated:\\n\\n- **Definition of \\\"step\\\"**: one world-step = one `env.step()` call that advances all `N` agents by one transition. Action *sampling* is **not** counted. This is consistent with PettingZoo's `parallel_env.step` semantics and with JaxMARL's per-call `step(state, actions) -> state`.\\n- **JAX back-end = CPU**. With `gpu_enabled: false` we have no choice; literal \\\"GPU JaxMARL vs CPU PettingZoo\\\" is not testable here. I'll annotate the result to that effect.\\n- **PettingZoo run-time = NumPy / pure-Python (single env, no `subproc`, no vector wrapper)**. Adding `supersuit.vector` or `parallel` wrapping on the PettingZoo side would change what we're measuring; default is *no* wrapper.\\n- **Single env on both sides (no `vmap` batched rollouts)**. JaxMARL shines under `vmap(env.step)` over `B` parallel envs; that is a deliberate out-of-scope axis for this comparison and would be presented as a follow-up, since adding `batch_size > 1` to one side and not the other is unfair.\\n- **Action shape parity**: I'll pin to **discrete actions** (`Discrete(5)`) on both stacks \\u2014 PettingZoo `simple_spread_v2` style \\u2014 unless continuous parity can be confirmed for the specific JaxMARL release. If only continuous is mutually available, both stacks are run in continuous mode with matching action repeats.\\n- **Auto-reset policy**: manual reset between episodes on both sides; we exclude reset time from the SPS numerator but log it.\\n- **Warm-up**: first 5 episodes (in addition to the trial warm-up trial above) are thrown out; compile time is reported, not averaged in.\\n\\nUncertainties that would change the design if answered differently:\\n\\n- **Exact JaxMARL release & API surface**: construction signature and whether action_type is `continuous_actions=True/False` vs `action_type='continuous'` \\u2014 affects ability to match action space exactly. *(Network disabled; cannot confirm.)*\\n- **Whether JaxMARL's `SimpleSpread` is functionally identical to PettingZoo's `simple_spread` at the physics level** (force coefficients, collision rules). For SPS this doesn't matter, but if the question is ever broadened to \\\"do they behave the same\\\", it would.\\n- **CPU thread counts / BLAS thread pinning for JAX**: JAX's default intra-op parallelism vs NumPy's OpenBLAS thread count. Pin both to e.g. 1 thread per env instance to avoid using all 24 cores on a single env and skewing the per-step latency comparison. This decision materially changes reported numbers.\\n- **Whether to permit PettingZoo MPE's `render_mode='rgb_array'` in the timed window**: default is `None`; if someone left it on or it auto-initializes a renderer, it dominates time. I'll forbid render and assert `render_mode is None`.\\n- **`max_cycles` identicality across stacks**: both default to 25 in PettingZoo; need to confirm JaxMARL's `SimpleSpread` constructor default matches. If they differ, I will pass `max_cycles=25` explicitly to whichever side needs it (and document).\\n- **Jit + `lax.scan` auto-batched mode**: the JaxMARL docs often show a `batch_size` argument at the `make_env` level; I need to confirm whether this is exposed by the MPE env specifically. If yes, Mode B will include a `B \\u2208 {1, 32, 128}` side-sweep as an additional informational curve; if no, Mode B stays at `B=1` and I won't fabricate the knob.\\n\\nPlease confirm: (a) the JaxMARL version tag to pin, (b) action parity choice (discrete v2-style on both, or continuous), and (c) sweeping `N` or holding `N=3`. Once those are fixed I will produce the full design (controls, exact loop pseudocode, environment-locking parameters, statistical aggregation, and the exact metric definitions and exclusions).\", \"evidence\": \"Concrete findings from `inspect_repository` / `execute_check` on the task workspace:\\n- `/workspace` contains only `task.json` (verified via `ls -la /workspace` and `find /workspace -type f`); no `jaxmarl/`, `pettingzoo/`, `mpe/`, READMEs, or docs are present on disk.\\n- `python3 -c 'import jax, jaxlib, numpy'` \\u2192 ModuleNotFoundError for `jax`, `jaxlib`, `numpy`. `pip3 list` confirms none of `jax`, `jaxlib`, `jaxmarl`, `pettingzoo`, `mpe`, `numpy` are installed. The environment spec is consistent: `\\\"software_environment\\\": \\\"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\\\"`.\\n- `pip3 show pettingzoo mpe jaxmarl` \\u2192 \\\"WARNING: Package(s) not found\\\".\\n- `nproc` \\u2192 24; `/proc/cpuinfo` \\u2192 \\\"Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 9 285K\\\"; `gpu_enabled: false` in the task environment map. So any JAX run defaults to the CPU back-end and may compete with PettingZoo for the same physical cores \\u2014 a material caveat for the comparison.\\n- Workspace metadata inside `task.json`: `\\\"documents\\\": {\\\"track.md\\\": \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"}` \\u2014 confirms this turn is documentation-only.\\n- Network disabled in the environment spec, so API/version claims for the two libraries cannot be verified against source from this workspace; they are stated as candidates to be pinned and are flagged in the uncertainties section accordingly.\\n- Entry-point naming for the canonical modules (`jaxmarl.environments.mpe.SimpleSpread`, `pettingzoo.mpe.simple_spread_v3` `parallel_env`) and standard constructor parameters (`num_agents`, `num_landmarks`, `max_cycles`, `continuous_actions`) are drawn from widely-documented public knowledge of these libraries; since source/README is not on disk and network is disabled, these names are presented as proposals to confirm, not as verified facts from a local clone.\\n- Action-space definition: PettingZoo MPE `simple_spread_v3` defaults to continuous actions (`Box(0,1,(5,))`), `simple_spread_v2` to discrete (`Discrete(5)`); JaxMARL MPE historically discrete with newer ports exposing both \\u2014 flagged as a parity decision that must be locked before the full design.\", \"assumptions\": [\"One world-step = one env.step() call that advances every agent by one transition; action sampling is excluded from the timed region.\", \"JAX back-end is forced to CPU because gpu_enabled is false; results will be annotated accordingly.\", \"Both stacks run a single environment instance (no vmap batching / no SuperSuit vector wrapper) for the apples-to-apples headline; batched parallel JAX rollouts are scoped to a follow-up mode.\", \"Manual reset between episodes on both stacks; reset cost is excluded from SPS numerator but logged.\", \"Action-shape parity will be pinned by reducing both stacks to discrete (PettingZoo v2 style) unless the researcher confirms the JaxMARL release exposes continuous actions with identical action dimension to PettingZoo v3.\", \"Warm-up of 5 episodes is discarded before timing; JAX compile time is reported separately, not folded into SPS.\", \"5 independent trials per cell with distinct outer seeds; 200 timed episodes per trial; report mean \\u00b1 std and per-trial min/max.\", \"Per-instance thread counts will be pinned (single-threaded per env) so the 24-core CPU allocation does not give either stack an inadvertent parallelism boost that masking Python/JAX dispatch overhead would otherwise create.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact JaxMARL release tag and whether its SimpleSpread accepts continuous_actions / action_type kwargs that match PettingZoo v3 shape \\u2014 would shift the parity decision in section 3.\", \"Whether JaxMARL SimpleSpread physics (force model, collision rules) is bit-for-bit equivalent to PettingZoo's \\u2014 does not affect SPS but would affect any sanity-check of state trajectories.\", \"Whether the JaxMARL MPE SimpleSpread wrapper supports a batch_size / vmap env-batching flag and what name it uses \\u2014 affects whether a batched-mode side-sweep is included in the design.\", \"Confirming PettingZoo render_mode defaults to None in this runtime so that renderer construction does not silently dominate the timed region.\", \"Whether jax.config.update('jax_platforms', 'cpu') is required versus relying on no-GPU autodetection, given CPU affinity 24 and absence of `nvidia-smi`/CUDA libs.\", \"Default max_cycles in the JaxMARL SimpleSpread constructor (does it match PettingZoo's 25?) \\u2014 if not, will pass it explicitly.\", \"Whether JAX's intra-op thread default of 1 (modern jax) is respected or whether jax.config.update('jax_num_threads', \\u2026) / xla flags need explicit pinning for the benchmark fairness argument.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ed7754a9-f9b0-4f21-9937-d4b974118931", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
